  "title": "Density bounds for Hausdorff measure (Simon 3.26, with 2.4–2.6)",
  "statement": "For every metric space X, real n ≥ 0 and Hⁿ-measurable A ⊆ X: (1) if Hⁿ(A) < ∞ then Θ^{*n}(Hⁿ, A, x) ≤ 1 for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ A; (2) if Hⁿ_δ(A) < ∞ for every real δ > 0 then Θ^{*n}(Hⁿ_∞, A, x) ≥ 2^{−n} for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ A.",
